{{Compendium/Extract|Ancient Shield}}
Ancient Shields are [[Shield]]s constructed from the [[Ancient Technology]] of the [[Sheikah]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> They were designed by [[Robbie]] to give the [[Hylian]] [[Champion]] [[Link]] a shield specifically engineered to guard against powerful [[Guardian]] lasers. Ancient Shields can only be made at the [[Akkala Ancient Tech Lab]]. Once the "[[Robbie's Research]]" [[Side Quest]] has been completed, the [[Ancient Oven]] will sell them to Link for 1,000 [[Rupee]]s, 10 [[Ancient Gear]]s, 1 [[Giant Ancient Core]], and 15 [[Ancient Spring]]s.<ref>{{Cite|Exchange for Ancient Shield?|Ancient Oven|BotW}}</ref> They belong to the [[Ancient Soldier Gear]] equipment archetype.<ref>{{Cite Book|quote= |book= CaC |publisher= |page= 175}}</ref>

When raised in defense or mounted in [[Link's House]], its surface emits [[Ancient Energy]]. Enhanced functionality allows it to deflect Guardian lasers without the use of a [[Perfect Guard]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> However, unlike a Perfect Guard, this automatic deflect function reduces the Shield's [[Durability]]. Despite this, Link can still perform a Perfect Guard to manually deflect Guardian lasers.

The base defense strength of Ancient Shields is 70, same as the [[Royal Guard's Shield]], though with superior Durability as well as its automatic laser deflect function. They are also superior to the [[Guardian Shield++]] in both defense strength and Durability. As a result, they effectively render both Guardian Shields++ and Royal Guard's Shields obsolete. However their defense and Durability are inferior to the mighty [[Hylian Shield]]. Additionally, while their defense is superior to the [[Daybreaker]] and [[Hero's Shield]], both have higher Durability. This shield also boasts 80% less friction while shield surfing, causing it to go much faster than other shields. The only other shields with this mechanic are [[Shield of the Mind's Eye]] and [[Radiant Shield]].

Being made from Ancient Technology, Ancient Shields will float if they are dropped in [[Water (Terrain)|Water]]. They will not burn when exposed to [[Fire]] or a [[Scorching Climate]], nor can they be picked up with the [[Magnesis]] [[Rune]]. Finally, Ancient Shields are unable to conduct [[Electricity]] or attract [[Lightning]] during [[Thunderstorm]]s.

